        "original_id": "a3db360a-cb87-5281-b544-b6ced6203655",
        "text": "This chunk is about:\n- People: Simon Wincer, Patrice Leconte, Walter Farley, Steven Farley\n- Works: The Young Black Stallion, Beauties at War, La guerre des Miss\n- Places: Sydney, France\n- Roles: film director, film producer, actor, comic strip writer, screenwriter, novelist\n\nFacts:\n- Simon Wincer was born in 1943 in Sydney and is an Australian film director and film producer.\n- Patrice Leconte was born on 12 November 1947 and is a French film director, actor, comic strip writer, and screenwriter.\n- The Young Black Stallion was directed by Simon Wincer.\n- The Young Black Stallion is based on the 1989 novel of the same name by Walter Farley and his son Steven Farley.\n- Beauties at War was originally titled La guerre des Miss in French.\n- Beauties at War was directed by Patrice Leconte and aired in France on 9 January 2009.",
